One thing is that the print in "generated quantities" block does not work in RStan since that part is done during writing sample to the CSV files, which is optional in RStan (I reported in another thread).  Actually, this is not work well for Stan during the warmup phase if the warmup sample is not saved.

$ more a.stan
parameters {
  real y;
}

model {
  y ~ normal(0, 1);
}

generated quantities {
  real chi;
  chi <- y * y;
  print("chi=", chi);
}

$ ./a --iter=4
STAN SAMPLING COMMAND
data = (specified model requires no data)
....
gamma = 0.05

Iteration: 1 / 4 [ 25%]  (Adapting)
Iteration: 2 / 4 [ 50%]  (Adapting)
Iteration: 3 / 4 [ 75%]  (Sampling)
chi=0.000855889
Iteration: 4 / 4 [100%]  (Sampling)
chi=0.000855889

--
Jiqiang

