> The one would be nice if it's faster than calling the above
> and then Cholesky factoring it:
>
>     // return lower tri Cholesky factor L distributed as lkj_corr(LL'|theta)
>     matrix cholesky_lkj_corr_matrix(double theta, size_t K);

OK, I'll do both of those. And yes, the essential tragedy of corr_matrix and cov_matrix is that we have functions that construct primitive Cholesky factors, but inevitably end up multiplying the Cholesky factors together to get the symmetric matrix and then often end up Cholesky factorizing that product. I think we should prioritize getting a Cholesky factor type (not necessary square, possibly row-normalized) into Stan for the next release.

Ben

