> On Sunday, March 17, 2013 4:11:14 PM UTC-4, Bob Carpenter wrote:
>
>     If we really want to start recruting more developers,
>     we're going to need to figure out some process to manage
>     the design and integration of the various parts.  It's
>     a qualitatively different game when there are more than two or
>     three people working on a project and the various pieces can't
>     be made wholly modular.
>
>
> Git was designed for Linux kernel development and is used by many projects with hundreds of developers and gigabytes of
> source code. So, I think we can handle it. The problem as I see it is that we have not fully abandoned cvs / svn
> workflows. If someone has an idea for how to do something, they should make a branch, implement the idea, and submit a
> pull request. And it won't get pulled until we are sure it doesn't break what already works.
>
> Ben
