> No.  The call to grad_log_prob (with double args) you have below
> calls the var version in order to compute the gradients and the
> log prob.
>
> To figure this out, you need to look where the function is
> defined (grad_log_prob, that is), then check what it calls.
> You'll see the var version getting called.

Sure, sure, sure.  I have no problem with the implementation (I had originally not noticed that the double version of log_prob and grad_log_prob were virtual but not pure virtual, hence my confusion).  When I try to use the double call on a model implementation, however, the virtual function does not get called; instead the compiler tries to coerce the vector<double> into a vector<var> and call the var versions directly.

I haven't pulled the recent template updates, so given that things are changing I'll just try to work around it.

