Most of them are errors, like the sampleP name, that I thought I had already fixed or simply missed.  I'll address any ambiguities inline.

The breaking up the files was also on my mind.  Do we want to keep to a strict one class/one file schema or can I put VERY related classes together.  The only example I can think of right now would be unit_metric_hmc and adapt_unit_metric_hmc, since the latter is only a small extension of the first.

> Michael is using a very different coding style than the
> rest of Stan -- how much do we care about this kind of
> thing?  I'd volunteer to restyle it, but I don't want to
