clang++ still works OK on our macs.  But it could
easily work differently under linux.  I believe what
is happening is that some of the old c lib functions
get automatically brought into global scope on some
platforms.  We're not explicitly qualifying them so as
to use argument-dependent lookup where we need to for
our auto-diff vars.

We just need to add explicit using statements in the
scopes where fabs gets used (NOT namespace scope -- restrict
as locally as possible within a function).

We only tracked this down because of the weird behavior we were
getting from lgamma at one point.

- Bob

